i'm not in favor of these special cases. the way it works now, it confirms
your choice to do something the gods might find distasteful. you'd want the
code to protect you from your mistakes.

if the interface has the wrong feel for you (i.e. the speed of the overlay
code in your case) you could make allowances for it (type slower) or find
a more suitable platform.

oh yeah, they eye freezes you with its gaze at first look. you remain
frozen even if you or the eye disappears because of what you've seen
previously. it's not continual gazing that keeps you frozen.

